      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design URL shortener service",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design URL shortener service",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2PYcRNQJkoA89bS0x0TLo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 280.35612389061725,
      "y": 209.48046875,
      "width": 888.984375,
      "height": 1750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 272285572,
      "version": 1481,
      "versionNonce": 516772228,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1742813021684,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional requirements:\n\n1. User provides long URL and system returns unique short URL \n2. The short URL redirects back to the long URL\n3. User can pass optional Expiration time\n4. User can pass optional alias \n\nNon functional requirements:\n\n1. Highly available - redirection should always work + creation of URL\n2. Eventual consistency - its fine if it takes a few seconds for URL to be shortened\n    - show pending status\n3. Scalable - 100M DAU and 1 B URLs\n5. Low latency redirection (< 100ms)\n\nBack of the envelope calculation:\n\n    Storage:\n    1. 1 B URLs\n    - 8 + 6 + 400 + 8 + 10 + 8 ~ 500B * 1B - 500GB\n    - 500 GB * 3650 ~ 500 * 3.6 TB ~ 2000 TB for 10 years\n\n    Throughput (TPS):\n    1. write: 10^9 / 10^5 - 10k TPS ~ 50k TPS\n    2. read: 1: 100 -> 5000k TPS\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. Url\nurlId: PK, UUID\nshortUrl: varchar(7)\nlongUrl: varchar(400)\nexpirationTime?: timestamp\nalias?: varchar(10)\nuserId: FK, UUID\ncreatedAt: timestamp\n\n2. User\nuserId: PK, UUID\nname\nage\ndob: timestamp\nisActive: boolean\ncreatedAt: timestamp\n\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. POST /api/v1/short-url\nRequest body\n{\n    \"longUrl\": \"\",\n    \"expirationTime?\": \"\",\n    \"alias?\": \"\"\n}\n\nResponse \n{\n    \"longUrl\": \"\",\n    \"expirationTime?\": \"\",\n    \"alias?\": \"\",\n    \"shortUrl\": \"\"\n}\n\n2. GET {domainName}/{shortUrl}\n- \n302 temporary redirect ✅\n301 permanent redirect\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional requirements:\n\n1. User provides long URL and system returns unique short URL \n2. The short URL redirects back to the long URL\n3. User can pass optional Expiration time\n4. User can pass optional alias \n\nNon functional requirements:\n\n1. Highly available - redirection should always work + creation of URL\n2. Eventual consistency - its fine if it takes a few seconds for URL to be shortened\n    - show pending status\n3. Scalable - 100M DAU and 1 B URLs\n5. Low latency redirection (< 100ms)\n\nBack of the envelope calculation:\n\n    Storage:\n    1. 1 B URLs\n    - 8 + 6 + 400 + 8 + 10 + 8 ~ 500B * 1B - 500GB\n    - 500 GB * 3650 ~ 500 * 3.6 TB ~ 2000 TB for 10 years\n\n    Throughput (TPS):\n    1. write: 10^9 / 10^5 - 10k TPS ~ 50k TPS\n    2. read: 1: 100 -> 5000k TPS\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. Url\nurlId: PK, UUID\nshortUrl: varchar(7)\nlongUrl: varchar(400)\nexpirationTime?: timestamp\nalias?: varchar(10)\nuserId: FK, UUID\ncreatedAt: timestamp\n\n2. User\nuserId: PK, UUID\nname\nage\ndob: timestamp\nisActive: boolean\ncreatedAt: timestamp\n\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. POST /api/v1/short-url\nRequest body\n{\n    \"longUrl\": \"\",\n    \"expirationTime?\": \"\",\n    \"alias?\": \"\"\n}\n\nResponse \n{\n    \"longUrl\": \"\",\n    \"expirationTime?\": \"\",\n    \"alias?\": \"\",\n    \"shortUrl\": \"\"\n}\n\n2. GET {domainName}/{shortUrl}\n- \n302 temporary redirect ✅\n301 permanent redirect\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
